{
  "schema": "stdo.context-generation.constraint-map/1",
  "scenario": "S2",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "S2-01",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The fictional migration relates three independently owned Products: SchemaKit, InvoiceBatch and InvoiceConsole. All select the exact methodology basis in BASIS.json. They share a workspace only for convenience; the cross-Product relation is migration-M14.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-02",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The owner asks to prepare the next bounded unit toward M14: compatible locale-field migration across a shared API and both consumers. The request is not to complete all Products in one Worker invocation.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-03",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Current SchemaKit source is schema-r12; its prior cut was schema-r11. The old published SchemaKit API 1.8 remains immutable. Proposed API 2.0 is an unaccepted candidate, not yet released or adopted.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-04",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Requirement M14-R1 says new API-2 producers emit locale as either a nonempty BCP-47 string or explicit null. Null means not supplied. Existing API-1 messages without locale must remain readable by both consumer successors.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-05",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "M14-R2 forbids treating absent or null locale as an empty string or choosing a machine-local default. It requires preservation of the original invoice amount and identifier.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-06",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "M14-R3 requires the two consumers to continue accepting the supported API-1 fixture population, and to agree on locale meaning for API-2. It does not require arbitrary malformed or future-version messages to be accepted.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-07",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Accepted design M14-D3 puts the wire normalization in SchemaKit codecs; consumers use its exported decode result. It selects SchemaKit contract/codec candidate first, followed by independently owned consumer adaptations and composed compatibility assessment.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-08",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The API-2 candidate wire schema is /fictional/schema-kit/specification/api/v2.json at schema-r12. The supported API-1 fixture set is /fictional/schema-kit/exports/fixtures/v1/ at fixture-v1-6. No file bytes beyond these declared facts are included in this exercise.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-08"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-09",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "At schema-r11 the consumer-normalization example incorrectly turned omitted API-1 locale into an empty string. The accepted schema-r12 contract corrects that API-1 example to null, without changing the amount/identifier rule. The supplied facts do not specify API-2 decoder behavior for an omitted locale field; API-2 producers must still emit it under M14-R1.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-10",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "InvoiceBatch source batch-r31 has not changed since a prior review; its candidate currently branches on empty-string locale. InvoiceConsole source console-r18 is also unchanged and already distinguishes missing locale from nonempty locale.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-11",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Review B-R9 assessed exact batch-r31 against schema-r11, passed amount/identifier preservation and accepted the then-selected locale interpretation. Its receipt names both subjects. No assessment of batch-r31 under schema-r12 exists.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-12",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "Review C-R4 assessed console-r18 with API-1 fixture-v1-6 only. Its scope excluded API-2. The retained passing observations identify those exact fixtures and the unchanged Console source.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-13",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The migration ledger has open obligations for API-2 locale semantics in both consumers, cross-consumer agreement, current independent review and composed compatibility. It has no accepted claim that all M14 obligations are discharged.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-14",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The fictional SchemaKit owner has admitted contract SC-12 for a Worker to edit only /fictional/schema-kit/src/codec.py, /fictional/schema-kit/tests/test_codec.py and /fictional/schema-kit/work/SC-12/RETURN.md. It allows reads of SchemaKit requirements, accepted M14-D3, current schema, supported fixtures and exported consumer compatibility requirements.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-15",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "SC-12 does not grant reading or editing either consumer implementation. Approved consumer exports are /fictional/invoice-batch/exports/compatibility.md at batch-export-4 and /fictional/invoice-console/exports/compatibility.md at console-export-3. Their provider-to-SchemaKit read edges are present for this work.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-16",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The InvoiceBatch owner has separately authorized a later candidate adaptation of /fictional/invoice-batch/src/decode.py and its tests, conditional on an identified SchemaKit candidate and exported contract. This is a different Worker territory and has not been activated.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-17",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The InvoiceConsole owner has authorized reading its export and planning the adaptation, but has not authorized source edits. A pending owner message is not a resolved grant.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-18",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The Executive can inspect the three owners’ requirements, exports, admitted contracts and named evidence receipts, and issue within the granted contracts. It has no implementation-write grant. No actor inherits another actor’s read edge from the Executive’s access.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-19",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The required independent reviewer is separate from the candidate author. It may read the exact SchemaKit candidate, requirements, design, fixture exports and named review/attempt receipts, run in-memory checks and write only /fictional/schema-kit/work/SC-12/REVIEW.md. It may not edit code, tests or the governing contracts.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-20",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The mandatory compatibility population for SC-12 includes an API-1 missing-locale case, API-2 null, API-2 nonempty locale, amount/identifier preservation, and refusal of API-2 empty-string locale. A green unit total without those predicates is not the specified result.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-21",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "An earlier staging fixture-registration attempt ST-6 timed out after submitting registration key fixtures-M14. Its client timeout alone did not establish the remote outcome. The attempt and key are retained rather than discarded.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-22",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The retained reconciliation REC-ST-6 is a stipulated current authoritative fixture fact: the registration committed once, its exact receipt was found, the registered fixture was then removed by the authorized cleanup actor, and a final read confirmed absence at staging revision stage-19. These observations cover ST-6’s only physical effect.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-23",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "A distinct staging-operator contract permits one new fixture registration for the selected SchemaKit candidate after binding REC-ST-6 and confirming staging is still at stage-19. SC-12 has no network or staging mutation grant. The present context-generation exercise must not perform that operation.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2-24",
      "kind": "scenario_fact",
      "text": "The current target is a locally reviewable candidate and explicit successor obligations; release publication and consumer adoption are outside all supplied grants. Results belong to the named per-Product carriers and feed the M14 Executive; a changed dependency or staging revision is a reason to reconsider the affected continuation.",
      "source_refs": [
        "/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/STDO_CONTEXT_GENERATION_001/inputs/S2.md@sha256:cee7db0c5d4c21a4f8b8fa1d80b4deb966896e20c8081bf35185dfe49abcb617#S2-24"
      ]
    },
    {
